      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Provider**\n\nI'm currently focused on selecting a concrete external provider for the Python script. The goal is to build a `stream_platform_generation.py` file that can stream output from a managed model platform. This code should keep the provider's response objects intact and use a single, well-defined provider to ensure clear identification within the program.\n\n\n**Defining the Framework**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Vertex AI as the managed model platform provider and will be leveraging its Python SDK for the task. The plan now involves outlining the `stream_platform_generation.py` file, incorporating the `google.cloud.aiplatform` library to initiate streaming requests to a Vertex AI model. The code will explicitly show how to iterate through responses, keeping the provider's response objects.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863191870,
          "start": 1789863188212
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc28d6f4001C0RRPsCpmQTwLF",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc28d2a40018FwUq5Pi2VmQta",
      "session_id": "ses_f43d72d6dffedEYR4l0bPGz7cP",
      "time_created": 1789863188212,
      "time_updated": 1789863191870
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "LyufjqCJWx3YzQ3H",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "\nimport google.cloud.aiplatform as aiplatform\nfrom google.oauth2 import service_account\nimport os\n\n# Set your Google Cloud project ID and location\nPROJECT_ID = os.getenv(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID\")\nLOCATION = os.getenv(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION\", \"us-central1\")\n\n# Initialize Vertex AI\naiplatform.init(project=PROJECT_ID, location=LOCATION)\n\ndef stream_model_generation(prompt: str, model_name: str = \"gemini-pro\"):\n    \"\"\"\n    Streams output from a managed model platform (Google Vertex AI)\n    while preserving provider response objects.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not PROJECT_ID:\n        raise ValueError(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID environment variable not set.\")\n\n    # Load the generative model\n    model = aiplatform.preview.generative_models.GenerativeModel(model_name)\n\n    print(f\"Sending prompt to {model_name}: {prompt}\\n\")\n\n    # Start streaming generation\n    responses = model.generate_content(\n        contents=[prompt],\n        stream=True\n    )\n\n    full_response_content = \"\"\n    for response in responses:\n        # Each 'response' is a provider-specific object (google.cloud.aiplatform_v1beta1.types.GenerateContentResponse)\n        # You can access its attributes, e.g., 'candidates', 'usage_metadata'\n        \n        # Access the text part of the response\n        if response.candidates and response.candidates[0].content and response.candidates[0].content.parts:\n            text_part = response.candidates[0].content.parts[0].text\n            print(text_part, end=\"\", flush=True)\n            full_response_content += text_part\n        \n        # You can also inspect the full response object for more details\n        # For demonstration, let's print a part of the raw response object\n        # print(f\"\\nRaw response object type: {type(response)}\")\n        # print(f\"Safety ratings: {response.candidates[0].safety_ratings if response.candidates else 'N/A'}\\n\")\n\n    print(\"\\n\\n--- End of Stream ---\")\n    return full_response_content\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    test_prompt = \"Tell me a short story about a brave knight and a wise dragon.\"\n    stream_model_generation(test_prompt)\n",
            "filePath": "stream_platform_generation.py"
          },
